   476→        <section className="section">
   477→          <h2>Feature Catalog</h2>
   478→          <p>
   479→            Comprehensive list of all rendering capabilities organized by category. Click to expand and see detailed feature descriptions with links to documentation.
   480→          </p>
   481→
   482→          <details style={{ marginTop: '2rem', border: '2px solid #2E7D32', borderRadius: '8px', overflow: 'hidden' }}>
   483→            <summary style={{ background: 'linear-gradient(135deg, #2E7D32 0%, #1B5E20 100%)', color: 'white', padding: '1.5rem', fontSize: '1.25rem', fontWeight: 600, cursor: 'pointer', userSelect: 'none' }}>
   484→              View All Engine Capabilities (26 Features)
   485→            </summary>
   486→
   487→            <div style={{ padding: '2rem', background: 'white' }}>
   488→              {/* Category 1: Core Rendering */}
   489→              <div style={{ marginBottom: '3rem' }}>
   490→                <h3 style={{ color: '#2E7D32', fontSize: '1.5rem', marginBottom: '0.5rem', paddingBottom: '0.5rem', borderBottom: '2px solid #2E7D32' }}>1. Core Rendering</h3>
   491→                <p style={{ color: '#666', marginBottom: '1rem' }}>Fundamental drawing operations: shape rasterization, edge-list algorithm, Porter-Duff compositing.</p>
   492→                <ul style={{ lineHeight: 2, color: '#555' }}>
   493→                  <li><strong>Edge Rasterization</strong> – Scanline algorithm using sorted edge list for efficient pixel coverage</li>
   494→                  <li><strong>Rectangle Drawing</strong> – Optimized axis-aligned rectangle fill with clipping</li>
   495→                  <li><strong>Polygon Drawing</strong> – Convex polygon rasterization using edge walking</li>
   496→                  <li><strong>Porter-Duff Blending</strong> – 12 compositing modes including src-over, xor, multiply</li>
   497→                  <li><strong>Polygon Clipping</strong> – Sutherland-Hodgman algorithm for viewport clipping</li>
   498→                </ul>
   499→              </div>
   500→
   501→              {/* Category 2: Shaders & Textures */}
   502→              <div style={{ marginBottom: '3rem' }}>
   503→                <h3 style={{ color: '#2E7D32', fontSize: '1.5rem', marginBottom: '0.5rem', paddingBottom: '0.5rem', borderBottom: '2px solid #2E7D32' }}>2. Shaders & Textures</h3>
   504→                <p style={{ color: '#666', marginBottom: '1rem' }}>Shader pipeline: solid colors, gradients (linear, radial, sweep), bitmap textures with tile modes.</p>
   505→                <ul style={{ lineHeight: 2, color: '#555' }}>
   506→                  <li><strong>Solid Color Shader</strong> – Simple constant color shader with alpha channel support</li>
   507→                  <li><strong>Linear Gradient</strong> – Color interpolation along a line with multiple color stops</li>
   508→                  <li><strong>Radial Gradient</strong> – Circular gradient radiating from center point</li>
   509→                  <li><strong>Sweep Gradient</strong> – Angle-based gradient (atan2) for color wheels</li>
   510→                  <li><strong>Bitmap Shader</strong> – Texture mapping with clamp, repeat, and mirror tile modes</li>
   511→                  <li><strong>Shader Composition</strong> – ProxyShader and ComposeShader for chaining transformations</li>
   512→                </ul>
   513→              </div>
   514→
   515→              {/* Category 3: Transformations */}
   516→              <div style={{ marginBottom: '3rem' }}>
   517→                <h3 style={{ color: '#2E7D32', fontSize: '1.5rem', marginBottom: '0.5rem', paddingBottom: '0.5rem', borderBottom: '2px solid #2E7D32' }}>3. Transformations</h3>
   518→                <p style={{ color: '#666', marginBottom: '1rem' }}>2D affine transformations: translate, rotate, scale, shear. Current Transformation Matrix (CTM) stack for hierarchical transforms.</p>
   519→                <ul style={{ lineHeight: 2, color: '#555' }}>
   520→                  <li><strong>Matrix Transform</strong> – 3x3 homogeneous coordinate matrix for 2D affine transforms</li>
   521→                  <li><strong>CTM Stack</strong> – save() and restore() for hierarchical transformation management</li>
   522→                  <li><strong>Translate</strong> – Move coordinate system by (dx, dy)</li>
   523→                  <li><strong>Rotate</strong> – Rotate coordinate system by angle (radians)</li>
   524→                  <li><strong>Scale</strong> – Scale coordinate system by (sx, sy)</li>
